So a few years back, my wife and her mother planned a trip to go to a women's retreat together.

91
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:05,000
And a couple of weeks before this women's retreat, my mother in law had bought a brand new vehicle.

92
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,000
It was the first like new vehicle that she had in a long time.

93
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:12,000
It had all of the bells and whistles and screens and technology.

94
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:18,000
And so she had planned to come pick Marissa up and they were going to drive together to the women's retreat.

95
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:25,000
And a couple hours before she was supposed to pick Marissa up, she called me and she was in a panic.

96
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:32,000
And the reason that she was in a panic is because she had driven two hours in the wrong direction.

97
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Now, how did she drive two hours in the wrong direction?

98
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Well, she drove two hours in the wrong direction because she had this new navigation system in her car.

99
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,000
She thought she had put in the coordinates.

100
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:48,000
And so when she left the house, she knew the way to go for the first hour or two hours.

101
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,000
And so she she was headed in the right direction for a while.

102
00:23:52,000 --> 00:24:02,000
And then what happened is she looked down and she started to follow the red line of her navigation system, which essentially the red line is just following the direction that she's headed.

103
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:05,000
So she gets on the highway headed in the wrong direction.

104
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:13,000
But because she had thought that she'd put the navigation system in, she just kept looking down and she's like, I guess I'm going in the right direction.

105
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:18,000
And it took her a few hours to realize the mistake that had been made.

106
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:29,000
And the reason I share this story at the beginning of our message is because if we're not careful, it's really easy to drift from your intended direction.

107
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Oftentimes we get started in a direction.

108
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,000
We feel comfortable.

109
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,000
We know where we're headed.

110
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:39,000
But if we don't keep a close eye on the direction that we're headed, we can easily drift.

111
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:42,000
And last week, Matt asked us to consider this question.

112
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:48,000
He said, what is it that you want in your relationship with Jesus in 2024?

113
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,000
And what do you need to focus on to get there?

114
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:52,000
What direction are you headed?

115
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:58,000
And what do you need to do to ensure that you get to the direction that you hope to get to?

116
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,000
This week, I want to take that question.

117
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,000
I want to expand it from the individual level to the church level.

118
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:11,000
See, when we sat down to create our mission, vision and values, essentially what we did is we answered this question that Matt asked last week.

119
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,000
Where do you want to go?

120
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Where, what are you hoping to get out of your, what are we hoping to get out of our church moving forward?

121
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:24,000
Our mission, vision and values is essentially the answer to that question.

122
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Where do we want to go?

123
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:36,000
And as we seek to follow Jesus together in this specific local church, this is where we want to go.

124
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:48,000
I said this last time I shared the mission, vision, values, but my belief is that every New Testament, Bible believing, Jesus loving church essentially has the same mission, vision and values.

125
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Our mission is the Great Commission to go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them and discipling them, teaching them to obey Jesus.

126
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Our values, our values are the New Testament ethics, all, almost every good Bible believing, Jesus centered church.

127
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:07,000
We all have the same mission and values.

128
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:15,000
However, each local church has a unique calling, just like individuals in the body have unique callings and spiritual gifts.

129
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:24,000
I believe each local church has a unique calling, a specific gift, a purpose that they get to play in their city for this time in history that they exist.

130
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:37,000
And so, yes, we're all about making disciples, baptizing, teaching our values are the values of the New Testament, but our written mission, vision values is kind of our attempt to focus.

131
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,000
What is it unique to us?

132
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:43,000
What is specific to our church that we feel called to do?

133
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:46,000
And the reality is this, there's no perfect church.

134
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:54,000
There are, you're never going to find a church that completely aligns with everything that you value.

135
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:57,000
We are by no means a perfect church.

136
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:05,000
But this mission, vision, value statement is our best attempt, our best effort to say together, this is where we're headed.

137
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,000
This is where we want to go as a church.

138
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:10,000
And so I'd love for you to consider these things.

139
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:12,000
I want you to love our church.

140
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:15,000
I want you to commit to our church and be a part of this thing together.

141
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:26,000
But as we share, if there are things that you're concerned about or don't like or all or just like, man, I don't know that I would that I'm super pumped about that thing.

142
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Man, this is what we're doing as a church.

143
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,000
And like we could use the space.

144
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:36,000
So like I'm not asking you to leave, but like don't try and take our church and make it your church.

145
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Like this is our church.

146
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,000
This is where we're headed together.

147
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,000
Let's do this thing together.

148
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:44,000
I asked you to consider, is this a church that you're willing to commit to?

149
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:49,000
I had a conversation with some people the other day that were talking about whether or not they wanted to become members.

150
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:52,000
And they were like, man, like we know membership is the serious investment.

151
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:57,000
And so we just want to take our time to make sure that this really is the church we want to plug into.

152
00:27:57,000 --> 00:28:02,000
I want that for all of you, because there's plenty of great churches in our city.

153
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:06,000
I am friends with many pastors in our city that have wonderful churches.

154
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:11,000
And so my goal here is not to say that our church is the right church, the best church.

155
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,000
This is just who we are.

156
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:14,000
We want you to be a part of it.

157
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,000
We're excited about it.

158
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:17,000
I personally love our church.

159
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:20,000
I would go to our church if you all didn't pay me to go to our church.

160
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:22,000
But it's not for everyone.

161
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:27,000
And so I might share some things today that you didn't know about our church or that make you uncomfortable.

162
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,000
That's OK.

163
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Let's talk.

164
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:33,000
My goal is not to grow our church, but to see God's kingdom grow on earth as it is in heaven.

165
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:38,000
OK, so the rest of our time, mission, vision, values.

166
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:41,000
And ultimately, I want to ask the question, how are we doing as a church?

167
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:48,000
And I want you to think, how am I individually living into this mission, this vision, this values?

168
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
So our mission, why do we exist?

169
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:53,000
What do we want to see happen as a church?

170
00:28:53,000 --> 00:29:01,000
We exist to invite real people with real lives into a Christ-centered community.

171
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:06,000
We exist to invite real people with real lives into a Christ-centered community.

172
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:09,000
If you ask me, this is a pretty catchy marketing phrase.

173
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:13,000
If I do say so myself, I was a part of helping create it.

174
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:16,000
So that's maybe a little bit self-centered.

175
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:19,000
But what does it actually mean, right?

176
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Like, what do we mean when we say this thing?

177
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:23,000
And really, there's two parts to our mission statement.

178
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:27,000
The first part is Christ-centered community.

179
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:33,000
In order for us to have some place to invite people, we first have to be creating a Christ-centered community.

180
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:39,000
The church exists to be the body of Christ to the world.

181
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:47,000
There's nothing worth inviting the world to if we aren't embodying the life-transforming power of the gospel together.

182
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:53,000
So first and foremost, if we are going to be successful as a church at doing the thing we say we want to do,

183
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:59,000
at going the direction we say we want to go, we have to be creating a Christ-centered community.

184
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:02,000
I love how St. Teresa of Avila says it.

185
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:06,000
She says, "Christ has no body, no body now but ours.

186
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Go and be Christ's body to the world."

187
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:11,000
This is what we want as a church.

188
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,000
We want to create a Christ-centered community.

189
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:20,000
A body of believers that embody the presence and power of the gospel of Jesus.

190
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Oftentimes the way we've preached the gospel in America, my opinion here,

191
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:31,000
it's so individualized that we've detached salvation from the body of Christ.

192
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:37,000
The reality is the gospel doesn't just reconcile us back to God, but it reconciles us back to one another

193
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:41,000
so that we can embody the message of the gospel of Jesus.

194
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:49,000
At Canvas, our top priority is that those who follow Jesus would pursue genuine, authentic community together.

195
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:55,000
That our lives and our relationships would embody the abundant life that Jesus has invited us into.

196
00:30:55,000 --> 00:31:05,000
I want our church to be an oasis of sacrificial, unconditional love, forgiveness, and acceptance in a world that's desperate for it.

197
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,000
So what does this look like?

198
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:17,000
I want to reread a passage in Romans chapter 12 that, in my opinion, is probably the clearest explanation for what I think a Christ-centered community looks like.

199
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:23,000
And if you will, just close your eyes as I read this passage or look at the words on the screen or whatever,

200
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:29,000
and focus in and just think like, man, what would it be like to be a part of a community like this?

201
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:35,000
And what might forming a community like this, what impact might it have on our city?

202
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:41,000
Romans 12:9 says, "Let love be without hypocrisy.

203
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Hate evil.

204
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Cling to what is good.

205
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Love one another deeply as brothers and sisters.

206
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Take the lead in honoring one another.

207
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Do not lack diligence and zeal.

208
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:55,000
Be fervent in the Spirit.

209
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,000
Serve the Lord.

210
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Rejoice in hope.

211
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:58,000
Be patient in affliction.

212
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Be persistent in prayer.

213
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Share with the saints in their needs.

214
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Pursue hospitality.

215
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Bless those who persecute you.

216
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:07,000
Bless and do not curse.

217
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Rejoice with those who rejoice.

218
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:10,000
Weep with those who weep.

219
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Live in harmony with one another.

220
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Do not be proud.

221
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,000
Instead, associate with the humble.

222
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Do not be wise in your own estimation.

223
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Do not repay evil for evil.

224
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:26,000
But give careful thoughts to do what is honorable in everyone's eyes.

225
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:34,000
And if possible, as far as it depends on you, live at peace with everyone."

226
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Wow.

227
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:41,000
I don't know about you, but I want to be a part of a community that embodies these truths.

228
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:50,000
And I believe that if we're going to do that, it starts with all of us as individuals focusing on Christ, cultivating a community that is centered around Christ.

229
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:54,000
So, how are we doing at creating a Christ-centered community?

230
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:58,000
Do our interactions with one another model the love of Jesus?

231
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Do our conversations in the lobby, at small group, team huddles, membership meetings, do they reflect the truths we just read in the Scripture?

232
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:18,000
This type of community, it's only possible when each of us as individuals pursue Christ with our whole mind and our whole heart, with all of our strength.

233
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Does that describe you?

234
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Does that describe me?

235
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:33,000
If we want to create a Christ-centered community, it starts with each and every one of us pursuing Christ together and then pursuing Christ in community.

236
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:40,000
And all of that, the goal of all of that is so that we can invite people into that Christ-centered community.

237
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:43,000
We believe that Christ is the power of God for life and salvation.

238
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:51,000
We want our friends, our coworkers, our family members, our neighbors, and yes, even our enemies to experience this transforming power.

239
00:33:51,000 --> 00:34:00,000
So, we intentionally invite people into our community so that they can explore the message of Jesus in a safe and welcoming environment.

240
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:13,000
The reality is for a long time in America, whether intentionally or unintentionally, churches kind of created this environment where people felt like they had to kind of fake it in order to feel welcome at church.

241
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:23,000
They had to come in, they had to put their best foot forward, they had to dress up in all of the nice clothes, they had to know all of the lingo, or at least pretend to know all of the lingo.

242
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:27,000
And the reality is at Canvas, like, we don't want that to be true.

243
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:36,000
We want to be a safe place for people who don't know Jesus, for people who are coming back to Jesus for the first time in a long time, for people who have no biblical knowledge whatsoever.

244
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:48,000
We want it to be a safe place for them to explore faith, to come into our Christ-centered community and see why the message of Jesus is so powerful, both for eternal salvation and for abundant life now.

245
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Jesus says this to those who would make it hard for people to feel welcome and follow Jesus.

246
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:57,000
In Matthew chapter 23, he says,

247
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:00,000
"Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites!

248
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:09,000
You are like whitewashed tombs, which look beautiful on the outside, but inside are full of bones of the dead and everything unclean.

249
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:18,000
In the same way, on the outside you appear to people as righteous, but on the inside you are full of hypocrisy and wickedness."

250
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:23,000
At Canvas, our goal is to create a safe place for real people with real lives to explore faith.

251
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:29,000
We want people to know that Jesus loves them as they are, and so do we.

252
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,000
But he loves them too much to stay there.

253
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:36,000
We want people to know that we know how flawed we are. We know how broken we are.

254
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:40,000
We are not trying to create some persona that we are amazing people.

255
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:43,000
We are broken in need of God's grace.

256
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:46,000
And we want this to be a safe place.

257
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:50,000
I had a conversation with somebody a couple Sundays ago.

258
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:53,000
It was just one of those in passing, "Hey, how are you doing?"

259
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:56,000
And this person said, "Well, you know, not really great."

260
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:58,000
And I was like, "Hmm, great, cool."

261
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:02,000
So I stopped and just kind of was like, "Okay, well, like, help me understand what's going on."

262
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:06,000
He's like, "Man, we're talking about all this stuff: hope, love, joy, peace."

263
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:12,000
He's like, "If I'm honest, it's really hard for me to really experience any of that right now."

264
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:18,000
And that was one of the most refreshing conversations I've had at church in forever.

265
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:22,000
And then a couple of guys that are friends with him heard, overheard the conversation we were having.

266
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:25,000
They swooped in and they said, "Dude, let's go to lunch. Let's have a conversation.

267
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:28,000
Like, don't go through this alone."

268
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:36,000
That is what we mean when we say that we exist to invite real people with real lives into a Christ-centered community.

269
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Are we becoming together a people of love who invite real people with real lives into a safe place to explore faith?

270
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Are we ourselves? Are we honest with ourselves? Are we honest with others about who we actually are?

271
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Are we creating a nonjudgmental and kind environment for those searching for God?

272
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:02,000
We exist to become like Christ together, to invite our friends, family, co-workers, and even our enemies

273
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:06,000
to experience the love and abundant life that comes from following Jesus.

274
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:08,000
We pray for them. We invite them.

275
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:16,000
For the longest time, I was intimidated by this passage in Scriptures where Paul says, "Follow me as I follow Christ."

276
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:21,000
I don't know about you, but that's a heavy statement to come out of anyone's mouth.

277
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:28,000
But the more I think about it, the more I realize that I think that really is the call of discipleship for every follower of Jesus.

278
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:32,000
May we be able to say, "Look, I'm doing my best to follow Jesus.

279
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:34,000
Why don't you follow me as I follow Jesus?"

280
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:37,000
We'll follow Jesus together.

281
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:40,000
Okay, so that's our mission statement.

282
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:43,000
And our vision statement is how do we measure success?

283
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:46,000
How do we know if we are doing this well?

284
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Our vision statement is this: to cultivate the kingdom of God on earth by proclaiming Jesus clearly and obeying Jesus boldly.

285
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:58,000
Again, another two-parter, so let's break it down first.

286
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Success for us looks like cultivating God's kingdom.

287
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:08,000
Our desire as a church is that we would play a small part in making God's kingdom more visible on earth as it is in heaven.

288
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:15,000
This is what Jesus tells us to pray for: pray that God's kingdom would come, that his will would be done on earth as it is in heaven.

289
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:20,000
We pray for that, and we seek to be a part of that happening in some small way.

290
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:24,000
We're more concerned with building the brand of Jesus than our own.

291
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,000
We want to see God's kingdom built.

292
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:29,000
If our church grows, great, but that's not our ultimate goal.

293
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:34,000
Our ultimate goal is that the name of Jesus would be made famous in our city.

294
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:40,000
The reality is our church has been experiencing consistent growth for the past few months.

295
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Our highest attendance Sunday was a few weeks ago.

296
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:48,000
There was 120 people more in this building than the first Sunday we met a little over a year ago.

297
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:52,000
That's amazing. We're so thankful for that. We're excited about that.

298
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:59,000
And with this type of growth, many churches in our situation would be having conversations about growth and expansion,

299
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:05,000
about how do we create more services? How do we raise money to buy a bigger building?

300
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:08,000
What do we do to accommodate this growth?

301
00:39:08,000 --> 00:39:19,000
And although none of those things are bad, the conversations that we've been having as a leadership team at Canvas is more about multiplication.

302
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:26,000
Because our vision isn't about growing our church. Our vision is about cultivating the kingdom of God in our city and on earth.

303
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:33,000
And so we've been having conversations about how can we use the growth that we're having and leverage it to plant churches,

304
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:41,000
to revitalize struggling churches, to strategically partner with other churches so that the kingdom of God can be made more visible in our city.

305
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:48,000
There are all kinds of churches around our area that are chasing after this together.

306
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:52,000
We're part of a pastor's prayer lunch where 12 to 15 pastors of other local churches.

307
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:55,000
We get together. We pray for one another. We partner with one another.

308
00:39:55,000 --> 00:40:00,000
There's a sense that the kingdom of God, that we are together as churches.

309
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Our women's retreat, I was talking to Jill last week.

310
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:08,000
She said that we had 32 women at our women's retreat from eight different churches.

311
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:12,000
This is success. This is what success looks like.

312
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:16,000
We want to see the kingdom of God cultivated in our city.

313
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:19,000
It's not about growing our church.

314
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:22,000
There's value in churches of every size.

315
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:27,000
Larger churches in our area have ministries and resources that allow them to do incredible things for the kingdom of God.

316
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:30,000
We are so thankful for these big churches in our city.

317
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:33,000
We love them and we partner with them.

318
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:41,000
However, we believe that that churches our size and smaller also bring a really strategic and important value to the kingdom.

319
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:46,000
And so we've just talked about, man, what would it look like instead of trying to become bigger and bigger and bigger?

320
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:55,000
What would it look like if we were a kingdom hub in our city that was sending people out to plant churches, sending people out to struggling churches to revitalize?

321
00:40:55,000 --> 00:41:01,000
The reality is our church is a result of creative partnerships and revitalization.

322
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:05,000
We are a church that was a merger of two churches.

323
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,000
It was a creative kingdom partnership.

324
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:14,000
As we look to the future, we just want to say, what if that is our legacy in this city?

325
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:26,000
What if our legacy is to creatively build relationships with other churches, to plant churches, to revitalize churches and to make strategic partnerships happen so that the kingdom of God can be more visible in our city?

326
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:33,000
That happens by the second part of our vision statement by proclaiming Jesus clearly and obeying Jesus boldly.

327
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:42,000
The gospel was, is, and will always be good news for the poor, opening the eyes of the blind and setting captives free.

328
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:49,000
The message of the gospel should never be void of tangible expressions of love to the marginalized and hurting in our community.

329
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:50,000
It's not just preach.

330
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:51,000
It's not just obey.

331
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:53,000
It's preach and obey.

332
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Serve, love, share.

333
00:41:57,000 --> 00:42:02,000
This is literally, it's literally the only thing the early church could find common ground on.

334
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:09,000
Peter and Paul, they were getting together to talk about Jews and Gentiles and how the whole early church was going to work.

335
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:12,000
And they were struggling to agree on just about anything.

336
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:15,000
But they finally were able to find unity.

337
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:20,000
And when they left in the midst of their unity, Paul says this in Galatians 2:10.

338
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:29,000
He said, "All they asked was that we should continue to remember the poor, the very thing I have been eager to do all along."

339
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:37,000
If we can't agree on anything else as a church, may we agree on obeying Jesus and proclaiming Jesus.

340
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:41,000
The gospel is to be both preached and lived, both heard and experienced.

341
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:44,000
How are we doing at this balance?

342
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:51,000
How are we proclaiming the message of Jesus with our words and obeying the message of Jesus with our lives?

343
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:57,000
I believe the more we genuinely and humbly proclaim the message of Jesus with our words and our actions,

344
00:42:57,000 --> 00:43:01,000
the more we will see glimpses of God's kingdom on earth as it is in heaven.

345
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:05,000
Okay, I think I'm, I don't know how I'm doing on time.

346
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:06,000
I don't think I'm doing great.

347
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:09,000
So I'm going to try and push through these core values.

348
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:15,000
The reality of this is that mission and vision that I just gave you is massive.

349
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:18,000
We could spend the rest of our lives chasing after that.

350
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:22,000
And really, it would be hard to know how well we were doing.

351
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:30,000
So what we did is we took four cultural values, four values that we believe if we commit to these four values,

352
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:33,000
it will help us produce our mission and our vision.

353
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:37,000
It's kind of shrinking things down to the smallest common denominator.

354
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:45,000
These four values, we believe if we actually get these right, that we will be able to move forward in our mission and our vision.

355
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:49,000
So number one, my favorite, I'll be honest with you, this is my favorite.

356
00:43:49,000 --> 00:43:50,000
All of them are great.

357
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,000
This is my favorite.

358
00:43:51,000 --> 00:43:54,000
We unite for the sake of the gospel.

359
00:43:54,000 --> 00:44:03,000
In order to remain focused on successfully creating a Christ-centered community that cultivates God's kingdom on earth above all else,

360
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:08,000
we hold secondary theology with an open hand.

361
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:13,000
Because the gospel is so important, we hold secondary theology with an open hand.

362
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:14,000
We unite for the sake of the gospel.

363
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:20,000
A Christ-centered community is only possible when we are laying down our preferences

364
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:24,000
to prioritize the gospel above everything else.

365
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
The reality is unity is at the heart of Christ's vision for his church.

366
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:32,000
In John 13, he says,

367
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:47,000
They will know you are my disciples by your love for one another.

368
00:44:47,000 --> 00:44:53,000
John 17, Jesus literally prays for you and me, for everyone who will follow Jesus after the disciples.

369
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:59,000
And he says, I pray that they will be one just as you and I are one if I'm honest.

370
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:05,000
As a pastor in the American church, I don't think we're great at prioritizing unity.

371
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:08,000
We get in intellectual arguments over secondary theology.

372
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:15,000
We get in intellectual arguments over our preferences of how we like to worship or the ministry philosophy that we prefer.

373
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:21,000
And at the end of the day, we've got to prioritize unity for the sake of the gospel.

374
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:28,000
The gospel is too important for us to get distracted by arguments with one another.

375
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:32,000
Look, this is my favorite.

376
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:35,000
And the reality is it's coming from somebody who loves theology.

377
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:41,000
I spent years of my life and a lot of my parents' money studying theology.

378
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:48,000
But what I've realized over the past 10 years is that if studying theology does not transform you into a person of love,

379
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:55,000
who seeks common ground with a diverse group of brothers and sisters in Christ, then it's all a waste.

380
00:45:55,000 --> 00:46:05,000
Some of the most unkind interactions I've had with people are people who are intellectually sure of their secondary theology.

381
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,000
Paul says this in 2 Timothy,

382
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:12,000
"Don't have anything to do with foolish and stupid arguments, because you know they produce quarrels.

383
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:19,000
And the Lord's servant must not be quarrelsome, but be kind to everyone, able to teach, not resentful.

384
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:23,000
Opponents must be gently instructed in the hope that God will grant them repentance,

385
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:26,000
leading them to a knowledge of truth.

386
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:30,000
Not saying that secondary theology isn't important or good.

387
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:40,000
Pursue the knowledge of the Scriptures, but do it in a way that produces humility and unity and kindness.

388
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:44,000
Please study the Bible. Form educated opinions. I have my own.

389
00:46:44,000 --> 00:46:50,000
But at the end of the day, we have to hold them with an open hand and a charitable spirit towards those we disagree with.

390
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:57,000
The one thing, the one thing I have little patience for is people who become convinced of their systematic theology without charity.

391
00:46:57,000 --> 00:47:03,000
They often ignore that there are godly people who are smarter than them on the other side,

392
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:08,000
who love the Scriptures, who love Jesus and have a different interpretation.

393
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:12,000
So in summary, the message of Jesus is good news to the poor.

394
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:15,000
It opens the eyes of the blind. It sets captives free.

395
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:22,000
It's far too important for you or me to let our preferred biblical interpretations or styles of worship get in the way.

396
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:24,000
There is one body of Christ.

397
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:29,000
So we intentionally lay down our preferences to unite for the sake of the gospel.

398
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:31,000
This has to be a mark of our church.

399
00:47:31,000 --> 00:47:40,000
If we're going to be about cultivating the kingdom of God, we got to unify around what matters most and and lay aside our opinions on secondary things.

400
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:45,000
Our next value is this. We rely on the living and written word of God.

401
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:52,000
I talked about this at the beginning, although we have some autonomy in defining our unique mission, vision and values as a church.

402
00:47:52,000 --> 00:47:57,000
Ultimately, all of this is guided by one thing and one thing only: the word of God.

403
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:02,000
We don't get to make up what we think is important in our culture.

404
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:08,000
The Scriptures and the life of Jesus and the teachings of Jesus tell us what should be our top priority.

405
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:13,000
2 Timothy 3 says that all Scripture is breathed out by God and profitable.

406
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:18,000
John 1:14 says that Jesus, the word, became flesh and dwelt among us.

407
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:23,000
At the end of the day, the decisions we make as a church and the direction we head as a church

408
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:29,000
is defined by what the Scriptures clearly teach and what is reiterated by the life and teachings of Jesus.

409
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:35,000
We are, will, and always will be. How did I? I messed that up.

410
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:41,000
We were, are, and will always be a Bible-trusting, Jesus-centered church.

411
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:51,000
The way I like to envision this with the Scriptures and Jesus being the living word, the Scriptures being the written word,

412
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:56,000
is that the Scriptures are our dartboard and the life and teachings of Jesus are our bullseye.

413
00:48:56,000 --> 00:49:01,000
Matt said this last week. He said that for him, the Sermon on the Mount is the canon within the canon.

414
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:05,000
It's the central focus of the life and teachings of Jesus.

415
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:12,000
And so we, we hone in on what's most important and the further out on the dartboard we get, the more open handed we are about those things.

416
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:21,000
So does our life reflect a total reliance on and obedience to what is clearly taught in the Scriptures

417
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:24,000
and reiterate it by the life and teachings of Jesus?

418
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:35,000
Is our church totally reliant on and obedience to what's taught in Scriptures and reiterate it in the life and teachings of Jesus?

419
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:41,000
Or do we pick and choose ideas from Scripture and Jesus that we like and ignore the parts that we don't?

420
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:43,000
May we never ignore the hard truths of Scripture.

421
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:48,000
May we be a church that totally relies on the written and living word of God.

422
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:51,000
Okay, number three, we prioritize real relationships.

423
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:55,000
I already spent a lot of time on this in our mission statement.

424
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,000
So I'm not going to beat a dead horse.

425
00:49:57,000 --> 00:50:00,000
I'll just say this, church is not an event we attend.

426
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:02,000
It is a community that we engage in.

427
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:05,000
You were never intended to follow Jesus alone.

428
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:09,000
You cannot grow in your faith in isolation or without authentic vulnerability.

429
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:15,000
You have to be willing to be honest with yourself and those around you as we pursue Jesus together.

430
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:18,000
James chapter five says it this way.

431
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:19,000
Is anyone among you in trouble?

432
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:20,000
Let them pray.

433
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:21,000
Is anyone happy?

434
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:23,000
Let them sing songs of praise.

435
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:24,000
Is anyone among you sick?

436
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:31,000
Let them call on the leaders, the elders of the church to pray over them and anoint them with oil in the name of the Lord.

437
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:35,000
And the prayer offered in faith will make the sick person well.

438
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:37,000
The Lord will raise them up.

439
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:39,000
If they have sinned, they will be forgiven.

440
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:45,000
Therefore, confess your sins to each other and pray for each other so that you may be healed.

441
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:48,000
The prayer of a righteous person is powerful and effective.

442
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:57,000
If we want to be a healthy, vibrant church, we have to intentionally pursue authentic and honest relationships with one another.

443
00:50:57,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Are you investing in authentic relationships aimed at being informed to the image of Jesus?

444
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:08,000
Am I investing in authentic relationships aimed at being informed to the image of Jesus?

445
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:13,000
Are you just showing up and consuming or are you plugging in and investing?

446
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:15,000
We prioritize real relationships.

447
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:18,000
Lastly, we cultivate spiritual gifts to serve others.

448
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:22,000
Church is primarily about giving of yourself for the good of the community.

449
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:28,000
Every follower of Jesus has spiritual gifts, talents, and callings that serve the whole.

450
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:32,000
The American church tends to view the church through the consumer lens.

451
00:51:32,000 --> 00:51:38,000
We want to fight back against this temptation by cultivating our gifts to serve others.

452
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:39,000
First Corinthians talks about it.

453
00:51:39,000 --> 00:51:40,000
I was going to read it.

454
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:41,000
I don't have time.

455
00:51:41,000 --> 00:51:46,000
It gives this illustration of the body that every part of the body matters.

456
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:50,000
Each one of you has something to offer to this church.

457
00:51:50,000 --> 00:51:53,000
No gift is more valuable than any other gift.

458
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:56,000
Every part matters.

459
00:51:56,000 --> 00:52:01,000
When we refuse to cultivate our gifts, the whole body misses out.

460
00:52:01,000 --> 00:52:06,000
A church is healthiest when all of the believers at that church understand their gifts

461
00:52:06,000 --> 00:52:10,000
and use them in accordance with the overall vision of the church.

462
00:52:10,000 --> 00:52:12,000
So do you know your gifts?

463
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:14,000
Do you understand who God has made you to be?

464
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:15,000
What he's calling you to do?

465
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
Are you using your gifts to cultivate the kingdom of God inside and outside the church?

466
00:52:21,000 --> 00:52:23,000
If not, let's talk.

467
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:25,000
I'd love to help you figure this out.

468
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:26,000
This is what I'm passionate about.

469
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:30,000
I'm passionate about equipping saints to do the work of the ministry.

470
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:33,000
Let me help you figure out what God's calling you to do.

471
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:41,000
Okay, so in conclusion, as we think about this common direction that we've laid out as a church,

472
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:44,000
this is where we want to go as a church.

473
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:48,000
We want to invite real people with real lives into a Christ-centered community.

474
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
We want to cultivate the kingdom of God on earth by obeying Jesus clearly and proclaiming Jesus boldly.

475
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,000
I might have flipped those around.

476
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:59,000
And we unite for the sake of the gospel.

477
00:52:59,000 --> 00:53:02,000
We rely on the living and written word of God.

478
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:08,000
We prioritize real relationships and we cultivate our gifts to serve others.

479
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:09,000
This is where we're headed.

480
00:53:09,000 --> 00:53:12,000
This is where we want to go.

481
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:19,000
My question for you is, is this something that you can get excited about?

482
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:24,000
Because we want our church to be excited about our mission, our vision, and our values.

483
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:27,000
If not, let me help you find a church that you can get excited about.

484
00:53:27,000 --> 00:53:30,000
Because again, we're all about cultivating the kingdom of God.

485
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:33,000
I'm okay if you would prefer to go somewhere else.

486
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:37,000
Again, we're not building our brand here.

487
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:43,000
If this is something you can get excited about, man, let's journey together.

488
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:49,000
Imagine what God can do through our church over the next few years if we stay committed to this mission together.

489
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:54,000
Last week, as Matt ended his sermon, he asked us to ponder this question.

490
00:53:54,000 --> 00:53:58,000
Where do we want to go in our relationship with God in 2024?

491
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:04,000
I was sitting at my in-law's house in their living room and as he asked me to ponder that question,

492
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:10,000
I was trying to get in a spot where I could just meditate on the question and think about what God wants for me

493
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:13,000
and ask the Holy Spirit to give me wisdom.

494
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:19,000
And there was a Christmas tree in the corner of the room and they had a star at the top of the Christmas tree.

495
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:25,000
That was like flickering lights glimmering at the top of the tree.

496
00:54:25,000 --> 00:54:31,000
And I just thought, okay, so that's where I'm headed with God.

497
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:35,000
I'm headed towards Jesus, conformed to the image of Jesus, focused on that.

498
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:42,000
And then below the star were all kinds of things that could distract me from keeping my gaze on the star.

499
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:47,000
There was red lights, green lights, blue lights, ornaments, family pictures, all kinds of things.

500
00:54:47,000 --> 00:54:54,000
And I just, I felt the Holy Spirit say, keep your eye focused on the star.

501
00:54:54,000 --> 00:54:57,000
Keep your eye focused on the primary thing.

502
00:54:57,000 --> 00:54:59,000
Pursue Jesus.

503
00:54:59,000 --> 00:55:02,000
Be conformed to the image of Jesus in 2024.

504
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:07,000
Don't get distracted by things that might be good, might be bad, might be neutral.

505
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:12,000
It doesn't matter. Keep your eyes focused on the star.

506
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:17,000
What I shared this morning is our church's north star.

507
00:55:17,000 --> 00:55:19,000
It's where we are headed.

508
00:55:19,000 --> 00:55:26,000
Let's focus on this together and let's be unwilling to be distracted by anything else.

509
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:36,000
There will be plenty of things, plenty of opportunities, plenty of exciting things that are going to cause us as a church to look away from the thing that we've decided we want to do.

510
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:46,000
My primary job as the pastor and your secondary job as invested members is to stay focused on this mission, vision and values.

511
00:55:46,000 --> 00:55:49,000
Call each other out when you see us stepping out of line.

512
00:55:49,000 --> 00:55:56,000
Our call as a church is too important to get distracted or to coast along.

513
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:59,000
Together, let's vigilantly commit to this direction.

514
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Let's stay focused on creating a Christ-centered community that we can invite our friends, neighbors, co-workers and even our enemies to.

515
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:13,000
So that the kingdom of God can be cultivated in the city of Winchester as it is in heaven.

516
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:15,000
Let's pray.

517
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:22,000
Father, I am so grateful for your word, for the wisdom and direction it gives to our lives.

518
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:29,000
I'm so thankful for Jesus, who is the word made flesh, dwelt among us, who showed us exactly how to live.

519
00:56:29,000 --> 00:56:40,000
Sacrificial enemy love, kindness, humility, patience and righteous anger towards the religious.

520
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
God, may we be a people who pursue Jesus together.

521
00:56:46,000 --> 00:57:01,000
God, may you supernaturally create a Christ-centered community here at our church that can be used to cultivate the kingdom of God through proclaiming Jesus clearly and obeying Jesus boldly.

522
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:05,000
God, may we take serious unity in the church.

523
00:57:05,000 --> 00:57:09,000
May we lay down our preferences in order to prioritize the gospel.

524
00:57:09,000 --> 00:57:13,000
May we be authentic and honest with one another about our struggles.

525
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:17,000
May we ask for prayer, for healing.

526
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:18,000
May we weep with those who weep.

527
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:20,000
Rejoice with those who rejoice.

528
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:24,000
God, may we understand the gifts that you've given us.

529
00:57:24,000 --> 00:57:26,000
May we use those to serve your church.

530
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:28,000
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

531
00:57:28,000 --> 00:57:29,000
Amen.

532
00:57:32,000 --> 00:57:33,000
Amen.

533
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:34,000
Amen.

534
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:31,980
Thank you.

535
00:58:32,000 --> 00:59:01,980
Thank you.

536
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:02,500
Bye.
